From: Jan Benedikt <karagos01@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 19:35:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] screenshot-manager: Finish a failed screenshot

When copying an output fails (phoc fails the copy while the output is
off, for example), maybe_screencopy_done() completes the D-Bus call but
never frees the frames. Every later screenshot is then refused as
"already in progress" until phosh restarts. A failed screenshot from
the keybinding also completes a NULL invocation.

Finish it through screenshot_done() instead: it completes the D-Bus
call or notifies about the failure, and frees the frames.
---
 src/screenshot-manager.c | 12 +++++++-----
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/screenshot-manager.c b/src/screenshot-manager.c
index 5f0e1e2..59d965a 100644
--- a/src/screenshot-manager.c
+++ b/src/screenshot-manager.c
@@ -823,12 +823,14 @@ maybe_screencopy_done (PhoshScreenshotManager *self)
   if (done + failed != self->frames->num_outputs)
     return;
 
-  /* With a failure no need to merge pixbufs */
+  /*
+   * With a failure no need to merge pixbufs. Finish the screenshot
+   * so that the next one can start: there is no clipboard copy to
+   * wait for.
+   */
   if (failed) {
-    phosh_dbus_screenshot_complete_screenshot (PHOSH_DBUS_SCREENSHOT (self),
-                                               self->frames->invocation,
-                                               FALSE,
-                                               self->frames->filename ?: "");
+    self->frames->copy_to_clipboard = FALSE;
+    screenshot_done (self, FALSE);
     return;
   }
 
